{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRIMARY AC SHIPPED — Gerrit change 1584 (2fa6-stash-create).\n\nWHAT LANDED\n_store/push.py no longer performs ANY refs/stash mutation. The stash push -> merge ->\nstash pop dance is replaced by the operator-approved design:\n\n    sha = git stash create        # writes a stash COMMIT OBJECT, does NOT touch refs/stash\n    git reset --hard -q           # create leaves the tree dirty; clear it ourselves\n    git merge <target>\n    git stash apply <sha>         # addresses OUR commit by sha; no stack consulted\n\nBecause the restore names a commit sha, it is unreachable from any other worktree's pop,\nand there is nothing to 'stash drop' afterwards (push.py:200 is gone). Verified: no\n'stash push' / 'stash pop' / 'stash drop' call sites remain in push.py.\n\nSemantics preserved: 'stash create' records tracked modifications + index state exactly\nas 'stash push' did, and neither touches untracked files; 'apply' without --index\nrestores unstaged, matching the old 'pop'.\n\nAC4 (_resolve_conflicted_pop's regenerable assumption) — ENFORCED, not assumed. Renamed\nto _resolve_conflicted_apply. It now classifies each conflicted path with\ngitutil.path_is_foreign_to_branch and routes both buckets through\ngitutil.discard_unmerged_paths: a path the tickets branch TRACKS is restored from HEAD\n(reconciler rebuilds it); a path it does NOT track cannot be ticket data, so it is\nremoved AND logged at warning level rather than vanishing silently.\n\nAC3 held-out test — tests/interfaces/store/test_push_shared_stash_2fa6.py. It encodes the\nRACE, not the steady state: LIFO ordering alone hides the bug because an uncontended pop\ndoes take its own push. The test injects a foreign source-worktree stash BETWEEN the\nset-aside and the restore. PROVEN RED on the parent commit (origin/main push.py): the\nraced stash is applied and src/raced.py materializes inside the store — the incident\nreproduced. GREEN on the fix, with the shared stack left byte-identical (both foreign\nentries still present, neither popped nor dropped).\nIt also asserts a non-conflicting dirty file returns byte-for-byte, which proves the tree\nwas genuinely RESTORED rather than merely reset away.\n\nGATES: make lint clean, mypy clean (491 files), 378 store tests pass. push.py is 792 LOC\n(was 758) — 8 lines under the hard cap, which is uncomfortably tight and is more evidence\nfor story 5e53.\n\nSTILL OPEN ON THIS TICKET (not delivered by 1584):\n- fsck invariant: report a tracker containing tracked-source paths (reuse\n  path_is_foreign_to_branch) so pollution is REPORTED, not only healed.\n- The supported maintenance entrypoint (backup ref BEFORE the first write; REFUSE when\n  rev-list origin/tickets..HEAD is non-empty; durable audit record).\n- The break-glass override + the docs rule ('no AD-HOC raw git; use the entrypoint').\nDo NOT close this ticket until those ship."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786380026554929001,"uuid":"0132fd7f-e47c-4cbe-9f21-42cdacf9bee0"}